{"name":"Private Eye","hex":"#006e89","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"private eye","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A private personal detective, employed to gather information about someone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/private_eye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Private investigator","blocks":[{"text":"A private investigator is a person who can be hired by individuals or groups to undertake investigatory law services. Private investigators often work for attorneys in civil and criminal cases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Detektiv.jpg/330px-Detektiv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Private_investigator","wikidata":"Q1058617"},{"title":"Private Eye","blocks":[{"text":"Private Eye is a British fortnightly satirical and current affairs news magazine, founded in 1961. It is published in London and has been edited by Ian Hislop since 1986. The publication is widely recognised for its prominent criticism and lampooning of public figures. It is also known for its in-depth investigative journalism into under-reported scandals and cover-ups."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Private_Eye_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Private_Eye","wikidata":"Q2195701"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm